      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="555" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The cDNA encoding the &amp;beta;-cyanolanine synthase (CAS) involved in the degradation of cyanide was identified and partially characterized in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. The molecular function was confirmed by recombinant expression of the gene in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; and by the specific inhibition of the enzyme using CAS-raised antibodies |CITS:[10889265]|.</Comment>
