  <Groups>
    <Group elementId="CPLX-1324" textLabel="CPLX-1324" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLX-1324" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="475" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>The SAT52 cDNA is able to functionally complement a serine acetyltransferase mutant strain of Escherichia coli. The SAT52 protein is a cytosolic SAT isoform, and is the only SAT isoform that is sensitive to cysteine feedback inhibition. Its catalytic product, O-acetylserine, is utilized directly in cysteine synthesis. Mitochondrial and plastidial isoforms of serine acetyltransferase also exist in Arabidopsis. The individual contribution of each isoform to cysteine synthesis is unkown. It has been proposed that, like bacteria, the plant cycteine synthase complex consists of one tetrameric serine acetyltransferase and two dimeric O-acetylserine (thiol) lyases. Co-expression of both protein coding genes in E.coli and subsequent protein purification detected a bi-enzyme complex.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLX-1324" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="SAT" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT5G56760-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="1" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-1644" />
      <Property key="^coefficient" value="4" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation__9048879_" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation__9692924_" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation__12063244_" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation__9830017_" />
    </Group>
    <Group elementId="CPLX-1326" textLabel="CPLX-1326" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLX-1326" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="555" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>The Arabidopsis genome contains nine OAS-TL genes. OAS-TL A1, B and C are the three most expressed OAS-TL genes and the activities of the three isoforms have been characterized.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLX-1326" />
